-- title:
--   ℓ-power torsion of Pic⁰ of the q-expansion function field
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ for a prime $p$, and let $\Gamma$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$. Write $F =$ [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) for the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $K((q))$ generated over $K$ by all elements of the form $\iota(p_f)/\iota(p_g)$, where for some weight $k \in \mathbb{Z}$ the forms $f, g$ are modular forms of weight $k$ for the image of $\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ admitting integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g \in \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$, $\iota$ denotes coefficientwise reduction into $K$, and $\iota(p_g) \neq 0$. Assume there is $x \in F$ transcendental over $K$ with $F$ finite-dimensional over the subfield $K(x)$ generated by $x$. Let $\ell$ be a prime whose image in $K$ is non-zero, i.e. $\ell \neq p$. Then for every $n \in \mathbb{N}$ the group of $\ell^n$-torsion elements of $\mathrm{Pic}^0(F/K)$ — degree-zero elements of the group of finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued functions on the places of $F$ over $K$, modulo principal divisors — is finite of cardinality $\ell^{2gn}$, where $g = \dim_K H^1(0)$ is the repartition-theoretic genus of $F$ over $K$.
--
--   This is the function-field form of Weil's count of the $\ell$-power torsion of the Jacobian of a curve of genus $g$ in characteristic $p \neq \ell$, equivalently the statement that the $\ell$-adic Tate module is free of rank $2g$, applied to the reduced $q$-expansion function field attached to an arbitrary subgroup $\Gamma \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$. It is used to show that an endomorphism of the $\ell$-divisible torsion coming from a degeneracy pair has the surjectivity needed in Ribet's isogeny step.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_abelJacobiCard_genusFF_qExpFunctionFieldC.lean

